WEBVTT

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:17.740
"The left side and the right side
of that country didn't get along,

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.740
so they built a wall...

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:28.240
and agreed not to have
dealings with each other."

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.790
Don't you think this is pointless, Madam Witch?

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.910
What do you mean by pointless?

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:46.240
Those on the two sides of the wall
really do not get along,

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.290
and do not want to see each other.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:51.490
But the wall itself is pointless.

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:52.790
Huh...

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:55.950
We don't want to lose to the other side.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.370
Even with this pointless wall,

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:01.160
we want to brag that
we are better on this side, but...

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.290
Do you have any ideas for
what we could do, Madam Witch?

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.200
Well, I might.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.450
Mr. Official, do you have a knife?

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:11.990
Hm? I do...

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:16.240
What are you planning to do with that?

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.160
This...

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:27.580
Hm?

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:32.870
"This side of the country is great.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:34.160
This side of the country is great

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:34.160
By the Witch of the Travels

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:34.910
By the Witch of the Travels."

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:36.910
What is the meaning of this?

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:41.410
This wall represents the
separation between the two sides,

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:46.290
but it also represents how
this side is wonderful, right?

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:48.290
Huh? Well...

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:53.700
So you should have travelers who
visit carve words into the wall like this.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.700
The more words you have on this side,

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:59.870
the clearer it is that this side is wonderful.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.700
But I don't really like doing things that way...

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.620
Oh, speaking of which,

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.120
on the other side of the wall,

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:10.080
many travelers have already left their marks!

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:17.450
"After that, I went to
the other side of the wall..."

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:19.120
Oh, speaking of which,

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:20.660
on the other side of the wall,

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:24.080
many travelers have already left their marks!

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.080
What?

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:29.490
"...and told them the same thing.

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:33.450
Since then, it became custom for
all travelers who visit that country

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:39.240
to etch words into that wall."

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:16.040
The Wall Etched by Travelers

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:20.990
What was the point in having
travelers carve words into the wall?

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.540
Well...

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:25.290
Maybe it was like a popularity contest.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:26.870
Popularity contest?

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:29.200
They want to brag that they're better

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.990
than the people on the other side of the wall.

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:35.830
To be able to say that there are
more words on their side praising them.

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:40.160
So then, in the end, which side was better?

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:44.580
Which side of the wall had more words on it?

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.910
You'll have to go see with your own eyes.

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:47.990
Yeah!

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:50.700
When I become a witch and travel...

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.910
Definitely!

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:55.080
Wow, this is amazing.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:56.660
"This country's the best!"

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:59.490
"I've never been to such a great country!"

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:02.080
"We'll be getting married soon!"

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:05.240
"Best traveling buds forever."

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:08.080
"Friends forever!"

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:16.580
This country is as
great as our muscles

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:19.870
Oh, excuse me, but...

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:23.910
You're the witch from the
United Magic Association, right?

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:26.040
I'm Saya, the Charcoal Witch.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:27.740
Nice to meet you!

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:31.990
I've heard about this wall,
but it really is amazing, huh?

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:36.330
You can really see how many
people have visited this country.

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:41.330
Our request for you is to do
something about this wall.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:42.990
Do something?

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.200
It's been more than ten years
since a traveling witch

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:49.040
suggested we have visitors
etch messages into the wall.

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:52.120
But recently, people have been losing interest,

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:54.410
so we want to do something new.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:57.870
Something new, huh?

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:02.830
It already seems pretty great to me, though.

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:06.620
The wall etched by travelers, huh?

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:08.830
Hm? Traveler?

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:14.290
Mister! Can I borrow a knife, please?

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:16.540
S-Sure...

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:21.870
...ve Mi... na... lo... Ela...

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:27.410
I ...ove ...iss ...lain... I love Miss Elaina...

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:35.830
Miss Elaina... Miss Elaina... Miss Elaina...

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.490
Wh-What are you doing?

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:41.910
This wall isn't a place for you
to carve your carnal desires!

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:44.490
What are <i>you</i> saying, Mister?

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.910
This is very important!

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:48.450
What's so important about that?

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:53.290
This wall is here for travelers to
carve how wonderful this country is!

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:55.160
Oh, about that rule--

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:57.330
Why don't you try changing it starting today?

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:58.950
What?!

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:04.790
Starting today, make it so the people
of this country can also carve into it.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:07.120
They can carve their passionate
feelings about the person they like,

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:08.870
or their hopes for the future,

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:11.160
or "I love Miss Elaina!" or something.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.910
What's the reason for doing that?

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:19.370
Hm? I mean, you're the ones
who made this wall, right?

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:23.290
So shouldn't it be here for your sakes?

00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:29.290
Turn it from a wall for travelers

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:33.660
into a wall that will help you
fix your eyes straight ahead.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.240
I see...

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:38.290
Thanks for this.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:39.740
Well, I'm off then!

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:41.540
Hm? Right...

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:44.950
I've got a job on the
other side of the wall, too!

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:03.330
Why was my heart swelling
with expectation on that day?

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:04.410
The answer is--

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:09.160
Because I was about to visit the country
with words etched into its wall

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:14.160
that appeared in The Adventures of Niké,
a book that influenced me greatly.

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:18.790
There's no wall here!

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:21.290
Welcome! Cheap wall pieces for sale!

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:24.080
How about some mementos of your trip?

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.910
This isn't just debris!

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:27.580
It's debris from the famous wall!

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:30.330
No, it <i>is</i> just debris...

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.330
It's rare! Rare!

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:32.700
Oh, you're the traveling witch!

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:34.790
It's been what, more than ten years?

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:38.080
You know who I am?

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:40.660
Your face looks younger than back then...?

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.330
It's true.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.490
Looking carefully, your chest is different, too.

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:45.740
It's true.

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:47.620
What, you're not her?

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:49.370
Too bad.

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:54.620
Well, are you two officials in this country?

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:57.870
Or are you just regular wrinkly old men?

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:00.120
We are indeed officials.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:03.580
But we are also wrinkly old men.

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:06.120
Then, this is perfect.

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:10.120
Will you tell me why you tore down the wall?

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:14.040
This is the explanation I was given--

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:19.490
At the advice of a witch who visited
this country a little before I had,

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:21.240
I love you! Forever!

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:24.410
the people of this country started
carving whatever they wanted on the wall.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.990
I hate that guy

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:24.750
The king has
donkey ears

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:27.370
At first, they were happy with that,

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:26.370
I am a fallen angel appearing from the deepest darkness

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:30.830
but as days and then weeks passed...

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:32.120
What does forever mean, anyway?

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.660
We already broke up!

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:37.620
I wrote something crazy when I was drunk!

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:41.200
What the hell? Who wrote
these insults about me?

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:41.200
People say, "What happens
on a trip, stays on a trip."

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:44.060
What <i>is</i> this? It's so embarrassing!

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:45.290
But the words etched by the people
of the country stayed with them,

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:50.200
and became embarrassing memories.

00:09:54.830 --> 00:10:00.160
And so, they decided to tear down the wall.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.910
Before they knew it,

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:04.910
the resentment they felt toward
the people on the other side

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:07.330
didn't matter anymore.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:13.790
Before, everyone thought they were better
than those on the other side of the wall--

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:17.120
But with the embarrassing
things they wrote themselves,

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:19.450
they realized that wasn't the case.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:23.410
In the end, this country didn't need a wall.

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:25.740
We were all the same in every way.

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:30.370
From now on, I suppose we will live
peacefully in our ordinary country.

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:31.700
Huh...

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:34.240
Well then, Madam Witch. Please excuse us.

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:35.830
Um--

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:42.370
Before the wall was torn down,
which side had more praises etched into it?

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:43.740
Isn't it obvious?

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:45.990
It was the same for both sides.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.830
The same?

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:50.120
We started off as the same country.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:55.330
And we all worked hard
so we wouldn't lose to the other side.

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:57.370
Why didn't you realize

00:10:57.370 --> 00:11:01.450
that the same growth was
happening on the other side of the wall?

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:04.370
In order to convince
ourselves that we were better,

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:06.990
we didn't want to look on
the other side of the wall.

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:09.370
Yeah, that went for all of us.

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:14.240
This
side
of
the
country
is
great.
By
the
Witch
of
the
Travels

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:18.370
I'm sure this worked out for the best.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:22.330
A country isn't for tourists or travelers,

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:25.410
but for those who live there.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:29.660
It's too bad I couldn't see the wall, though.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:33.490
I wonder if Niké carved those words

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:35.910
thinking the wall would be gone in the future.

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:38.290
No, there's no way.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:42.490
Cute witch, how about a piece
of the wall as a souvenir?

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:47.700
Well, I suppose as a memento,
I'll take... this one.

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:49.160
Thanks!

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:51.950
Please come again!

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:58.740
Elai...

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:01.790
Elai...?

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:22.950
Yes, this year's grapes look
like they're ripening well, too.

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:25.290
I'm sure they'll make delicious wine.

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:27.830
I'm looking forward to that.

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:29.200
Step, step...

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:30.700
Grandpa!

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:31.870
Look, look!

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:34.700
I'm going to wear this for the
Grape-Throwing Festival that's coming up!

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:37.660
Oh, it looks good on you.

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:41.950
Hey, Grandpa, how did the
Grape-Throwing Festival start?

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:44.740
How? Well...

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:49.700
A long, long time ago,

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:54.950
when this village was still split
into That Village and This Village,

00:12:54.950 --> 00:12:57.990
and all we did was fight,

00:12:57.990 --> 00:13:04.370
a witch came to visit during the grape harvest.

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:10.580
The Grape-Stomping Girl

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:15.580
Welcome to This Village.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:16.910
"This Village"?

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:20.490
Yes! Our village is called "This Village,"

00:13:20.490 --> 00:13:24.950
and on the other side
of the road is "That Village."

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:29.410
The two villages, This and That,
are famous for wine, right?

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:33.040
Indeed! Wine is a local specialty.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.700
Madam Witch, do you like wine?

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:37.410
I've never had any.

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:39.040
That's why I came here.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:39.950
Oh?

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:44.990
I wanted my first taste of alcohol
to be something very delicious.

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:49.540
I see. Then, you were
right to come to This Village.

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:50.870
The wine from This Village is so delicious,

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:53.660
the wine from That Village
and elsewhere cannot compare!

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:56.950
It is truly a wine made by God!

00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:58.740
It's that good?

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:00.700
So, is that the wine you boast of?

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:03.120
Gulp! No, it's not...

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:06.200
This wine is from That Village.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:13.410
I-It's outrageous!
That Village has started doing <i>this</i> !

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:17.410
"Grape-stomping maiden,
Rosemary, from That Village.

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:21.950
'I lovingly stepped on the grapes.'"

00:14:21.950 --> 00:14:25.830
With this wonderful label
of the lovely Rosemary,

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:28.990
That Village is increasing their sales.

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:30.040
Huh.

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:34.490
And they make it seem like Rosemary
is the place of origin of the wine--

00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:35.620
"Place of origin"?

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:36.700
That's right.

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:39.080
Not the manufacturer, but the place of origin?

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:43.160
Because making her the place of
origin will tempt people to buy it.

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:45.790
"Tempt"?

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:51.790
In other words, appealing to fetishes
is also important in business.

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:54.950
Huh, so it's selling well, is it?

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:58.080
Just because a cute girl
is stepping lovingly on it!

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:00.200
"Stepping lovingly"...

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:04.490
Then, why doesn't This Village
try competing with them

00:15:04.490 --> 00:15:08.290
by getting a cute girl to do
the, "stepping lovingly" thing?

00:15:08.290 --> 00:15:10.540
Well said!

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:12.080
That's exactly what we should do!

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:14.830
If we get a sweet maiden
to step lovingly on our grapes,

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:17.160
then we can win!

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:20.080
So, Madam Witch, will you do the honors?

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:21.990
Well?

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:22.910
Huh?

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:28.990
Everybody! Madam Witch said
she'll step lovingly on our grapes!

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:31.450
I can't believe such a cute witch
will step lovingly on our grapes!

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:34.040
All right! Step on me, too!

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:41.160
Um, what am I...

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:41.160
Hurry up and get ready!

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:43.740
Hey, wait--

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:55.040
Why do I have to wear this?

00:15:56.200 --> 00:16:00.830
Grape-stomping maidens
must all wear these clothes!

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:03.240
It makes them more tempting.

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:04.990
"Tempting"?

00:16:04.990 --> 00:16:07.450
Ready, go!

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:14.240
Oh my, what might you be doing?

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:20.370
Hello, Chief of This Village that's dying out.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:24.370
Y-You...! The shiningly beautiful Rosemary!

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:27.200
Rosemary...!

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:30.830
Oh? What might that bottle
you're holding to your chest be?

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:31.700
Gulp!

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:34.620
Might it be wine from my label?

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:37.790
Could you be a fan of mine?

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:41.330
F-Fan? O-Of course not...

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:44.700
I can sign the label if you'd like.

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:46.490
Sign?!

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:53.870
And? Who in the world is this undersized
girl in grape-stomping maiden clothes?

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:55.870
I'm a traveling witch.

00:16:55.870 --> 00:16:58.990
Oh? A witch?

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:02.540
Oh, I see. You can't beat me,

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:07.790
so you're planning to have this
thin girl step lovingly on some grapes?

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:09.450
"Thin," you say?

00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:12.410
Her face is just okay, too.

00:17:12.410 --> 00:17:14.660
"Just okay"?

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:17.410
Her figure is like that of a child's.

00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:19.700
"Like a child's"?!

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:23.080
No, not " <i>like</i> a child"--she <i>is</i> a child.

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:29.620
You can't beat me by having a child
like this step lovingly on grapes!

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:33.490
Well then, excuse me.

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:37.620
Step! Step! Step! Step!

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:40.240
Chief, I will do it.

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:41.660
Huh?

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:45.120
I will be the grape-stomping maiden!

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:47.870
Yeah!

00:17:54.120 --> 00:18:09.330
Die! Die! Die! Die! Die! Die!

00:17:54.120 --> 00:18:09.330
Step! Step! Step! Step! Step! Step!

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:17.910
I'm beat...

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:20.660
Madam Witch, good work.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:23.580
I feel like I stomped a lot of grapes today.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:26.490
How much wine do you think it'll make?

00:18:26.490 --> 00:18:30.450
Let's see... maybe about half a cask?

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:34.120
That's it? Even though I stomped that much?

00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:37.990
It's so hard being a grape-stomping maiden...

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:43.080
How much of that wine is being sold?

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:48.700
A lot! Hundreds, maybe
even thousands of bottles!

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:55.620
Do you mean to say that Rosemary is
stomping grapes from morning until night

00:18:55.620 --> 00:18:58.200
to make that many bottles of wine?

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:02.200
Don't you think it's strange?

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:04.450
It is...

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:30.490
Step! Step! Step! Step!

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:12.990
Step harder on those grapes.

00:19:12.990 --> 00:19:16.330
Don't you want to sell
wine with my label on it?

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:17.870
Come on! Come on!

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:23.450
What in the world...

00:19:23.450 --> 00:19:27.740
The wine wasn't lovingly
stepped on by Rosemary...!

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:30.490
Well, it's obvious now.

00:19:30.490 --> 00:19:31.700
Then--

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:41.580
This means the point of
origin is fraudulent, isn't it?

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:44.620
This is a case that could be brought to court!

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.290
Step...

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:48.200
Crap...

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.580
We're found out, huh?

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:51.240
We were selling so many, too...

00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:53.910
It's kind of amazing we weren't
found out until now, though.

00:19:53.910 --> 00:20:01.580
Rosemary's wine... was stomped
by those strong men over there...?

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:05.700
What's the big deal
about lying about the origin?

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:07.290
There's no difference once you drink it!

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:12.120
I see. It's my first time drinking wine,
but it really is delicious.

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:14.450
What's important are the feelings!

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:16.120
Even if it tastes the same,

00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:20.910
it was important for it to
be stepped on by Rosemary...

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:25.910
That's... That's what fetishism is!

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:29.080
Shut up! Don't complain about Rosemary!

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:30.200
Be quiet!

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:32.540
Bastard!

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:34.740
What are you doing to our chief?!

00:20:51.830 --> 00:20:56.620
Oh, really, what am I to do with you all?

00:21:14.990 --> 00:21:17.450
And then? And then what happened?

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:21.240
Everyone took those grape bullets...

00:21:24.120 --> 00:21:26.990
...and was knocked out.

00:21:26.990 --> 00:21:30.450
By the time we woke up,

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:34.160
the witch had already left.

00:21:42.990 --> 00:21:46.580
And that's the story of how
the Grape-Throwing Festival began.

00:21:46.580 --> 00:21:49.160
It was a good way to release stress,

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:52.870
so it became tradition
to have it during the harvest.

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:57.830
And before we knew it, the two villages
had stopped fighting and become one.

00:21:57.830 --> 00:22:01.620
Really? Then we need to thank that witch!

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:03.700
Yes, we do...

00:22:07.450 --> 00:22:10.580
What happened to Rosemary?

00:22:10.580 --> 00:22:11.910
That's--

00:22:11.910 --> 00:22:13.950
That's?

00:22:13.950 --> 00:22:17.120
Well, that's a story for another time.

00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:19.040
I think it's about time we had lunch.

00:22:19.040 --> 00:22:20.370
Go wash your hands.

00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:22.160
Okay!

00:22:22.950 --> 00:22:26.450
Really, ripening well...

00:22:26.450 --> 00:22:29.790
Tempting me no matter how old...

00:22:29.790 --> 00:22:34.120
Hey, good work! Let's have lunch now.

00:22:34.120 --> 00:22:35.910
Okay!
